% Tuple keys must be injective.  The first two rows below
% differ only in which side of the argument boundary a literal SUBSEP byte
% falls on, and the third spells the SUBSEP escape with a real backslash; with
% either escape missing from value_encode() they collapse into one tuple.
p("xq:y", "z").
p("x", "yq:z").
p("x\\Sq:y", "z").
